{"id":"u-8cb69655-42b6-4bb2-a930-9f9553641c65","src":"community","title":"Hardwood Hypertrophy","author":"Aravind B S","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/OGwuVQ-untitled-program","desc":"A high-yield, intermediate 3-day full-gym program built for a complete equipment setup. Designed for busy schedules with strict 60-minute morning workout sessions, this routine leverages a tailored Upper / Lower / Full Body split optimized specifically around your weekly timeline: 3 days of gym training (Monday, Wednesday, Friday), 2 days of active sports and cardio (Saturday, Sunday), and 2 days of recovery (Tuesday, Thursday).\n\n Program Breakdown & Weekly Structure:\n- ​Monday (Upper Body Aesthetics & Power): Focuses on chest width, upper back density, and shoulder caps to build a commanding V-taper frame.\n- ​Tuesday (Rest & Recovery): Complete physical rest to allow upper-body muscular repair and central nervous system recovery before lower-body training.\n- ​Wednesday (Lower Body Power & Knee Resilience): Targets quad mass, hamstring drive, and explosive vertical jump force while protecting joint integrity.\n- ​Thursday (Rest & Recovery): Dedicated rest day to ensure full lower-body recovery and glycogen replenishment.\n- ​Friday (Full Body Hypertrophy Polish): Balances total-body volume, lat width, and posterior chain strength right before your weekend activities.\n- Saturday & Sunday (Sports & Running): Dedicated to high-intensity sports performance, court agility, and cardio sessions without being weighed down by cumulative lower-body gym fatigue.\n\n​Core Objectives:\n- ​Size & Aesthetics: Maximizes hypertrophic gains for a lean, muscular frame at 6 feet tall.\n- ​Athletic Performance: Prioritizes posterior chain power, core stability, and single-leg strength essential for vertical jumps, sprinting, and quick directional changes on the basketball court.\n- ​Time Efficiency: Engineered for fast-paced, high-intensity 60-minute blocks to fit seamlessly into a morning rou